WIP / PoC: Add a kolla-ansible deployer image.

Kolla-Ansible is today installed onto the deploy host with pip, and
its Ansible collections are then fetched from Galaxy and git by
"kolla-ansible install-deps". The result depends on what those
sources serve on the day, on the host's Python, and on whatever is
already in the operator's ~/.ansible/collections, which is searched
before any system path. Two deploy hosts installed a day apart can
therefore run different code against the same cloud.

This change adds a kolla-ansible image which packages the deployment
tool itself, in the same way as Kolla packages every service.

